Description: Guard QQuickBorderImage::sciRequestFinished() against a null sciReply
 QQuickBorderImage::load() calls deleteLater() on d->sciReply and sets the
 pointer to nullptr whenever the source is re-evaluated. The reply's finished()
 signal can already be queued at that moment, so the slot may still run after
 the pointer has been cleared -- at which point it dereferenced a null pointer
 and terminated the process with SIGSEGV.
 .
 Reproducible on a multi-display setup: attaching a second screen re-evaluates
 the border image source while a .sci request is in flight.
 .
 Every other reply-finished handler in Qt Quick already guards against this
 exact case -- qquickanimatedimage.cpp uses "if (d->reply)" and
 qquickfontloader.cpp uses "if (reply)". QQuickBorderImage was the only one
 missing the check.
Author: OnePlus 8 Pro Ubuntu Touch port
Bug: shell SIGSEGV on DisplayPort hotplug
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-16
--- a/src/quick/items/qquickborderimage.cpp
+++ b/src/quick/items/qquickborderimage.cpp
@@ -467,6 +467,14 @@
 {
     Q_D(QQuickBorderImage);
 
+    // load() clears sciReply (after deleteLater()) whenever the source is
+    // re-evaluated, but a queued finished() from the old reply can still be
+    // delivered afterwards. Without this guard that is a null dereference.
+    // Matches the guards already present in QQuickAnimatedImage and
+    // QQuickFontObject.
+    if (!d->sciReply)
+        return;
+
     d->redirectCount++;
     if (d->redirectCount < BORDERIMAGE_MAX_REDIRECT) {
         QVariant redirect = d->sciReply->attribute(QNetworkRequest::RedirectionTargetAttribute);
